# The build-image workflow's offline checks run `git show -m --check` on the
# pushed commit; git's whitespace checker flags these paths falsely:
# - Patch files are themselves diffs. A blank context line is exactly one space,
#   which reads as trailing whitespace. setup.sh's `git diff --check` on the
#   applied SGLang tree is unaffected.
# - Chat templates are model input; their whitespace is load-bearing, so the
#   fix for a flagged line is never to strip it.
# - benchmarks/ and evals/ hold run receipts (server logs, profiler dumps) kept
#   verbatim; their whitespace is the tool's output, not an edit.
*.patch                   -whitespace
*.diff                    -whitespace
*.jinja                   -whitespace
patches/**                -whitespace
llmcompressor-patches/**  -whitespace
ream-patches/**           -whitespace
benchmarks/**             -whitespace
evals/**                  -whitespace
